{
  "platform_id": "u2c67bF9-OA",
  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:u2c67bF9-OA",
    "purpose": "A roundup of heavy wool outdoor jackets: a vintage Filson Double Mackinaw Cruiser, the Duckworth Snowcrest Shirt Jacket, the WeatherWool Al's Anorak and the creator's own Iron Snail Mammoth Jacket. It covers wool weights, construction, features and prices, with a short 'Wool School' on coarse versus fine wool. A planned Woolrich segment was cancelled because the jacket never arrived.",
    "video_type": "comparison",
    "thesis": "The creator presents several of the greatest heritage and modern wool jackets for rugged outdoor use, explains how wool type and weave affect toughness, softness and warmth, and introduces his own Mammoth jacket as a contender.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "The Woolrich hunting jacket segment was cancelled because the package was lost in the mail; it is promised for a future video.",
      "The Filson featured is a 1980s Double Mackinaw Cruiser bought on eBay, with a double layer of wool across the top including the sleeves (a built-in cape) and a rear map pocket; vintage age can be told from the Woolmark logo on the neck tag.",
      "The Duckworth Snowcrest is a $600 shirt jacket made from Rambouillet merino wool, with reinforced high-wear areas and bound inner seams; it is not a substitute for heavy outdoor jackets.",
      "Wool School: coarse wool (Filson, Mammoth) is very abrasion resistant but scratchy; fine wool is soft and drapes well but is less tough; long-staple fine fibers regain strength; finer fibers give a better warmth-to-weight ratio.",
      "WeatherWool uses its own jacquard-woven fabric; the Al's Anorak is $655, their shirt jac $550 and their CPO shirt $475. WeatherWool focuses on outdoor tops, while Duckworth focuses on base layers and wool-padded pieces.",
      "The Iron Snail Mammoth uses 28 oz double-layered wool, a lockable collar, corozo nut buttons, custom-knit storm cuffs, an 'odd duck' pocket with a snap clip, and a 9 oz worsted wool lining.",
      "Its 'windwall technology' is an internal cape-coat sandwich with the lining between the wool layers. The Mammoth retails for $550 versus $495 for the Filson Single Mackinaw, and a special edition in treadle-loomed Scottish wool is planned."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Intro and cancelled Woolrich segment",
        "summary": "Introduces the lineup of wool jackets and the criteria covered (weight, fit, insulation, lining, features). Explains that the Woolrich jacket never arrived, so its section is cancelled.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 0
      },
      {
        "title": "Filson Double Mackinaw Cruiser",
        "summary": "Covers a vintage 1980s Filson Double Mackinaw Cruiser from eBay: fabric weight, how to date it by the Woolmark tag, the double-layer cape construction, the map pocket, quality and high prices.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Duckworth Snowcrest Shirt Jacket",
        "summary": "Explains why the $600 Snowcrest disappoints anyone expecting a heavy jacket but excels as a shirt jacket. Covers its weight, its ranch-sourced Rambouillet merino wool, reinforced wear points and bound seams. Interrupted by a sponsor read.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Wool School",
        "summary": "Explains coarse versus fine wool: toughness and itch versus softness and drape, how long-staple fibers add strength, and why finer fibers give a better warmth-to-weight ratio. Closes the Duckworth discussion.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "WeatherWool Al's Anorak",
        "summary": "Discusses WeatherWool's jacquard-woven fabric, the Anorak's price alongside their shirt jac and CPO, and how WeatherWool and Duckworth target different uses.",
        "first_segment": 8,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "The Iron Snail Mammoth",
        "summary": "Presents the creator's own Mammoth jacket and its fabric, collar, buttons, cuffs, pockets, worsted wool lining and windwall construction. Covers price versus the Filson Single Mackinaw, pre-order timing and the special edition.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 19
      }
    ],
